  "findings": [
    "The early request first-second interval improves in both repeats and both orders:4Kpaired median reduction77.16\u201377.24%;1K4.94\u20135.19%. This tests one fixed native schedule.",
    "Later physicalslot15 first-second delay increases ~0.4ms. Ready-yield produces3 vs2 slot0outputs at1K and6 vs2 at4K, while slot15produces2 in both arms. Equal PF work therefore does not imply equal total decode work.",
    "Paired total completion median increases426\u2013441us at1K and1482\u20131582us at4K. This is the latency/fairness tradeoff observed by this fixture, not a throughput estimate.",
    "D-after-P paired decode-phase overhead at4K is29.30/53.24us across repeats;1K is-4.68/-4.24us. Repeat variation prevents assigning a fixed percentage of serving delay to kernel interference."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Native block with deterministic synthetic hidden rows; no tokenization, mux admission/cancellation, network transport, SSE or independent model-quality gate.",
    "Native-ready intervals and total walltime include ordered diagnostic input staging; phase durations exclude that staging. No eviction occurs betweenP andD.",
    "Cold policy arms execute different decode work and different physical extents. Actual rung is not exposed through the diagnostic API; no compacted-slot or exact-rung performance claim.",
    "Only Gemma12 layer5 full-attention block,1K/4K and two requests. Does not cover sliding attention, GDN, allmodels, fullnetwork, realserving or packed-prefill.",
    "Memory and numerical gates are the frozen internal D/P-D and reset checks; no raw independent output oracle was added."
  ],
